After picking up the raincoat, I go to the section with the shirts.
There are many types of shirts there.
I like a green-colored cotton shirt.
It is a beautiful shirt.
I check its size.
This is my usual size.
I go near the fitting room to try the shirt on.
But the line in front of the fitting room is very big.
I assume that this shirt will fit me perfectly.
Therefore, I don't try it on.
I take the raincoat and the shirt to the billing counter.
There are not many people there.
The line at the billing counter is smaller than the line at the fitting room.
The cashier rings up the bill for both items.
I pay the money.
He gives me the receipt.
I carefully put that receipt in my pocket.
